<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haojing</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haojing, or Hao, was the main capital of the Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a>, founded by King Wu on the east bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feng-river">Feng River</a> south-west of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xian">Xi'an</a>. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fengjing">Fengjing</a> on the opposite bank it formed the Zhou royal centre, known as Zongzhou. In 771 BCE the Marquis of Shen and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quanrong">Quanrong</a> sacked it and killed King You, and the court moved east to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chengzhou">Luoyi</a>, beginning the Eastern Zhou.</p></div>
